<%
box = infobox.InfoBox()
box.title = 'Download Ogg Vorbis RC2 Software For Unix/Linux'
box.fontsize = -1
box.title_image = '/images/NewsBox-bg.png'
box.title_image_r = '/images/NewsBox-right-bg.png'

self.write(box.start())
%>

<i>Note: If you use an rpm based distribution other than redhat, you can probably still use the RPMs
provided by download the SRPMS and rebuilding them (rpm --rebuild x.src.rpm)</i><br>
<br>
<i>Note to Debian users: Debian unstable is kept up to date with the latest packages you will find here.
After several days with no reported issues, these packages make their way to the testing branch.</i>

<h2>Player Plugins</h2>
<blockquote>
Player plugins allow your favorite media player to play Ogg Vorbis files.
<br><br>

<b><a href="http://www.xmms.org/">XMMS</a></b> (requires libraries: <b>libogg</b>, <b>libvorbis</b>):<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<A href="http://www.xmms.org/">Download at xmms.org</A><BR>

<b><a href="http://www.freeamp.org/">FreeAMP</a></b><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="http://www.freeamp.org/index.html?mode=download">download FreeAMP</a><br>

</blockquote>

<br>

<h2>Encoders / Players / Tools</h2>
<blockquote>
These tools will allow you to play, encode and manage Ogg Vorbis files.
<br><br>

<b>Vorbis Tools</b> (requires libraries: <b>libao</b>, <b>libogg</b>, <b>libvorbis</b>)<br><br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for RedHat Linux:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/vorbis-tools-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm">vorbis-tools-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm</a><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/vorbis-tools-1.0rc2-1.src.rpm">vorbis-tools-1.0rc2-1.src.rpm</a><br>

<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for everyone:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/vorbis-tools-1.0rc2.tar.gz">vorbis-tools-1.0rc2.tar.gz</a><br>

</blockquote>

<br>

<h2>Libraries</h2>
<blockquote>
These are the core libraries that make Ogg Vorbis work.  You'll need these
to use anything else.
<br><br>

<b>libao</b><br><br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for RedHat Linux:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libao-0.8.0-1.i386.rpm">libao-0.8.0-1.i386.rpm</a><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libao-0.8.0-1.src.rpm">libao-0.8.0-1.src.rpm</a><br>
<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<i>developer packages</i><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libao-devel-0.8.0-1.i386.rpm">libao-devel-0.8.0-1.i386.rpm</a><br>

<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for everyone:<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libao-0.8.0.tar.gz">libao-0.8.0.tar.gz</a><br>

<br>

<b>libogg</b><br><br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for RedHat Linux:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libogg-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm">libogg-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm</a><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libogg-1.0rc2-1.src.rpm">libogg-1.0rc2-1.src.rpm</a><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<i>development packages</i><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libogg-devel-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm">libogg-devel-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm</a><br>

<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for everyone:<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libogg-1.0rc2.tar.gz">libogg-1.0rc2.tar.gz</a><br>

<br>

<b>libvorbis</b> (requires libraries: <b>libogg</b>)<br><br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for RedHat Linux:<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libvorbis-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm">libvorbis-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm</a><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libvorbis-1.0rc2-1.src.rpm">libvorbis-1.0rc2-1.src.rpm</a><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<i>development</i><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libvorbis-devel-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm">libvorbis-devel-1.0rc2-1.i386.rpm</a><br>

<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for everyone:<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/rc2/unix/libvorbis-1.0rc2.tar.gz">libvorbis-1.0rc2.tar.gz</a><br>

</blockquote>

<br>

<h2>Python Bindings:</h2>
<blockquote>
If you wish to use or develop Ogg Vorbis software in Python, get these.
<br><br>

<b>pyao</b> (requires libraries: <b>libao</b>)<br><br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for RedHat Linux:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/beta4/unix/pyao-0.0.2-1.i386.rpm">pyao-0.0.2-1.i386.rpm</a><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/beta4/unix/pyao-0.0.2-1.src.rpm">pyao-0.0.2-1.src.rpm</a><br>

<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for everyone:<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/beta4/unix/pyao-0.0.2.tar.gz">pyao-0.0.2.tar.gz</a><br>

<br>
<b>pyogg</b> (requires libraries: <b>libogg</b>)<br><br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for RedHat Linux:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/beta4/unix/pyogg-0.2-1.i386.rpm">pyogg-0.2-1.i386.rpm</a><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/beta4/unix/pyogg-0.2-1.src.rpm">pyogg-0.2-1.src.rpm</a><br>

<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for everyone:<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/beta4/unix/pyogg-0.2.tar.gz">pyogg-0.2.tar.gz</a><br>

<br>

<b>pyvorbis</b> (requires libraries: <b>libogg</b>, <b>pyogg</b>, <b>libvorbis</b>)<br><br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;for RedHat Linux:<br>

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="files/beta4/unix/pyvorbis-0.2-1.i386.rpm">pyvorbis-0.2-1.i386.rpm</a><br>
